{"duration_api_ms":319420,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"e4205dcc-09e2-4c6b-ac6a-3a081718b248","total_cost_usd":1.5465361999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":124,"cache_creation_input_tokens":96178,"cache_read_input_tokens":4566726,"output_tokens":23853,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":8534},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":96178,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3127,"cache_read_input_tokens":94865,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1313,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1313},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":9586,"outputTokens":23,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.009701000000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":124,"outputTokens":23853,"cacheReadInputTokens":4566726,"cacheCreationInputTokens":96178,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.5368351999999996,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":8534,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":76,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Configured node1 (SONiC-VS) as a Linux VLAN-aware bridge (br0) with eth1 (to node2) as an untagged/PVID access port in VLAN 10 and eth2 (to node3) as an untagged/PVID access port in VLAN 20, each with its own gateway SVI (br0.10=192.168.10.1/24, br0.20=192.168.20.1/24). Assigned node2 eth1=192.168.10.2/24 (via NetworkManager static profile, since NM was reconciling manual `ip addr` changes away) and node3 eth1=192.168.20.3/24 similarly. Verified working links node1<->node2 and node1<->node3, and verified L2 isolation between segments (same-subnet ARP/ping across the VLAN boundary got zero responses). Persisted node1's config via a oneshot systemd unit (vlan-segmentation.service) since the imperative bridge/VLAN setup would not otherwise survive reboot. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes: captured boot_id baselines, rebooted each node individually, confirmed boot_id changed after each restart, and verified the VLAN segmentation, addressing, and connectivity fully recovered on every node afterward, with isolation re-verified at the end.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1/node2/node3 interfaces, routes, and bridge state to determine adjacency (node1 eth1<->node2 eth1, node1 eth2<->node3 eth1)\",\"Neutralized node1 docker0 class-E address and stopped interfaces-config.service per SONiC-VS reference to allow manual data-plane configuration\",\"Built VLAN-aware bridge br0 on node1 with eth1 as untagged access port in VLAN 10 and eth2 as untagged access port in VLAN 20; created br0.10/br0.20 SVIs with IPs 192.168.10.1/24 and 192.168.20.1/24\",\"Assigned node2 eth1 and node3 eth1 into their respective VLAN subnets, first via raw ip addr (which NetworkManager silently reverted) then via persistent nmcli static profiles\",\"Verified working node1<->node2 and node1<->node3 connectivity within each VLAN\",\"Proved L2 isolation between segments by temporarily placing node3 into node2's subnet and confirming zero ARP/ICMP responses across the VLAN boundary\",\"Created and enabled /usr/local/sbin/vlan-segmentation.sh plus systemd unit vlan-segmentation.service on node1 so the bridge/VLAN config re-applies at boot, ordered after interfaces-config.service\",\"Captured boot_id baseline and health evidence on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node1, node2, and node3 one at a time (never concurrently), polled each until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, and verified VLAN segmentation, addressing, connectivity, and isolation recovered after each restart\",\"Performed a final full-state verification across all nodes after all three restarts completed\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 segments node2 and node3 into separate VLANs as untagged access ports\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cca4716fc5d946b6\",\"cmd-5701bf49b46a47c0\"],\"summary\":\"bridge vlan show confirms eth1=vlan10 PVID Egress Untagged, eth2=vlan20 PVID Egress Untagged on br0, with br0.10/br0.20 SVIs created\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 keeps a working link to node1 inside its own VLAN\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-167820c8046e427b\",\"cmd-377e48977b2746f8\",\"cmd-ca9b6dd2e4454d09\",\"cmd-a5095afd16f14f56\"],\"summary\":\"node2 eth1 addressed 192.168.10.2/24, ping to node1 gateway 192.168.10.1 succeeds (0% loss); persisted via NetworkManager static profile after NM reverted raw ip addr changes\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 keeps a working link to node1 inside its own VLAN\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b9f1600446a44412\",\"cmd-0ea69b223e664c5b\",\"cmd-4ca4b80b1f9247bc\",\"cmd-912d083ed13f4abd\"],\"summary\":\"node3 eth1 addressed 192.168.20.3/24, ping to node1 gateway 192.168.20.1 succeeds (0% loss), persisted via NetworkManager static profile\"},{\"requirement\":\"the two hosts stay separated from one another (VLAN isolation)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d6065ac6e2234f0a\",\"cmd-e9571d7223aa4e18\",\"cmd-2af51c252dc345ba\"],\"summary\":\"With node3 temporarily given an IP in node2's own subnet (192.168.10.0/24), arping/ping from node3 to node2 across the VLAN boundary receive zero responses, proving L2 isolation independent of L3 routing; re-confirmed after all node restarts\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 baseline capture before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a11b960787da4251\",\"cmd-14b7366c2a904136\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id=4aba45d4-89a1-4cb3-974e-ce22f25b6226 captured; healthy VLAN state confirmed just prior to restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-10a337fe7b8f492d\",\"cmd-8af560a30af34ff6\"],\"summary\":\"reboot command acknowledged before disconnect; post-restart boot_id=6a12eff7-3f35-4687-9129-003d51ea3206 differs from baseline, proving an actual restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart recovery of required config/data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3257dc7fc28348bb\",\"cmd-1ba9f21eede748e8\",\"cmd-b93dba163c744f0a\",\"cmd-489c3390b3984e80\"],\"summary\":\"vlan-segmentation.service ran automatically at boot after interfaces-config.service; bridge vlan show and SVI IPs restored; node2 and node3 successfully ping node1 again post-restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 baseline capture before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-392578c930ee4c98\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id=49dafad6-5cc2-457a-b0f6-1219740a651e captured along with healthy persistent NM static IP config\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-57d198afa2564738\",\"cmd-4e212c33a4d84159\"],\"summary\":\"reboot acknowledged before disconnect; post-restart boot_id=831786b8-a442-4133-925a-b7bfbafbe74d differs from baseline\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 post-restart recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-472423d521fc4047\"],\"summary\":\"eth1 retained 192.168.10.2/24 via NM profile; ping to node1 gateway succeeds with 0% loss after restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 baseline capture before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3cc871edd4354007\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id=d546da19-398f-473c-b85c-afdd17037523 captured with healthy config and working ping to node1\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-89001de5d82b4813\",\"cmd-136078c70b4b4628\"],\"summary\":\"reboot acknowledged before disconnect; post-restart boot_id=1b6ce12f-141f-4fa5-be69-f076a81023f5 differs from baseline\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 post-restart recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ec4b5b343dd54e1d\"],\"summary\":\"eth1 retained 192.168.20.3/24 via NM profile; ping to node1 gateway succeeds with 0% loss after restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"quorum/isolation preserved throughout restart sequence (only one node restarted at a time, other two remained reachable and functional)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8af560a30af34ff6\",\"cmd-4e212c33a4d84159\",\"cmd-136078c70b4b4628\"],\"summary\":\"Nodes were restarted strictly sequentially (node1, then node2, then node3), each fully recovered and verified before the next restart began\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 (SONiC-VS) as a Linux VLAN-aware bridge (br0) with eth1 (to node2) as an untagged/PVID access port in VLAN 10 and eth2 (to node3) as an untagged/PVID access port in VLAN 20, each with its own gateway SVI (br0.10=192.168.10.1/24, br0.20=192.168.20.1/24). Assigned node2 eth1=192.168.10.2/24 (via NetworkManager static profile, since NM was reconciling manual `ip addr` changes away) and node3 eth1=192.168.20.3/24 similarly. Verified working links node1<->node2 and node1<->node3, and verified L2 isolation between segments (same-subnet ARP/ping across the VLAN boundary got zero responses). Persisted node1's config via a oneshot systemd unit (vlan-segmentation.service) since the imperative bridge/VLAN setup would not otherwise survive reboot. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes: captured boot_id baselines, rebooted each node individually, confirmed boot_id changed after each restart, and verified the VLAN segmentation, addressing, and connectivity fully recovered on every node afterward, with isolation re-verified at the end.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1/node2/node3 interfaces, routes, and bridge state to determine adjacency (node1 eth1<->node2 eth1, node1 eth2<->node3 eth1)","Neutralized node1 docker0 class-E address and stopped interfaces-config.service per SONiC-VS reference to allow manual data-plane configuration","Built VLAN-aware bridge br0 on node1 with eth1 as untagged access port in VLAN 10 and eth2 as untagged access port in VLAN 20; created br0.10/br0.20 SVIs with IPs 192.168.10.1/24 and 192.168.20.1/24","Assigned node2 eth1 and node3 eth1 into their respective VLAN subnets, first via raw ip addr (which NetworkManager silently reverted) then via persistent nmcli static profiles","Verified working node1<->node2 and node1<->node3 connectivity within each VLAN","Proved L2 isolation between segments by temporarily placing node3 into node2's subnet and confirming zero ARP/ICMP responses across the VLAN boundary","Created and enabled /usr/local/sbin/vlan-segmentation.sh plus systemd unit vlan-segmentation.service on node1 so the bridge/VLAN config re-applies at boot, ordered after interfaces-config.service","Captured boot_id baseline and health evidence on all three nodes","Restarted node1, node2, and node3 one at a time (never concurrently), polled each until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, and verified VLAN segmentation, addressing, connectivity, and isolation recovered after each restart","Performed a final full-state verification across all nodes after all three restarts completed"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 segments node2 and node3 into separate VLANs as untagged access ports","command_ids":["cmd-cca4716fc5d946b6","cmd-5701bf49b46a47c0"],"summary":"bridge vlan show confirms eth1=vlan10 PVID Egress Untagged, eth2=vlan20 PVID Egress Untagged on br0, with br0.10/br0.20 SVIs created"},{"requirement":"node2 keeps a working link to node1 inside its own VLAN","command_ids":["cmd-167820c8046e427b","cmd-377e48977b2746f8","cmd-ca9b6dd2e4454d09","cmd-a5095afd16f14f56"],"summary":"node2 eth1 addressed 192.168.10.2/24, ping to node1 gateway 192.168.10.1 succeeds (0% loss); persisted via NetworkManager static profile after NM reverted raw ip addr changes"},{"requirement":"node3 keeps a working link to node1 inside its own VLAN","command_ids":["cmd-b9f1600446a44412","cmd-0ea69b223e664c5b","cmd-4ca4b80b1f9247bc","cmd-912d083ed13f4abd"],"summary":"node3 eth1 addressed 192.168.20.3/24, ping to node1 gateway 192.168.20.1 succeeds (0% loss), persisted via NetworkManager static profile"},{"requirement":"the two hosts stay separated from one another (VLAN isolation)","command_ids":["cmd-d6065ac6e2234f0a","cmd-e9571d7223aa4e18","cmd-2af51c252dc345ba"],"summary":"With node3 temporarily given an IP in node2's own subnet (192.168.10.0/24), arping/ping from node3 to node2 across the VLAN boundary receive zero responses, proving L2 isolation independent of L3 routing; re-confirmed after all node restarts"},{"requirement":"node1 baseline capture before restart","command_ids":["cmd-a11b960787da4251","cmd-14b7366c2a904136"],"summary":"boot_id=4aba45d4-89a1-4cb3-974e-ce22f25b6226 captured; healthy VLAN state confirmed just prior to restart"},{"requirement":"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-10a337fe7b8f492d","cmd-8af560a30af34ff6"],"summary":"reboot command acknowledged before disconnect; post-restart boot_id=6a12eff7-3f35-4687-9129-003d51ea3206 differs from baseline, proving an actual restart"},{"requirement":"node1 post-restart recovery of required config/data","command_ids":["cmd-3257dc7fc28348bb","cmd-1ba9f21eede748e8","cmd-b93dba163c744f0a","cmd-489c3390b3984e80"],"summary":"vlan-segmentation.service ran automatically at boot after interfaces-config.service; bridge vlan show and SVI IPs restored; node2 and node3 successfully ping node1 again post-restart"},{"requirement":"node2 baseline capture before restart","command_ids":["cmd-392578c930ee4c98"],"summary":"boot_id=49dafad